description: Shared Minecraft agent contract and task-specific workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow the repository's `AGENTS.md`. Use `dev/agent-workflow.md` for the
shared Codex/Cursor development loop, commands, and validation evidence.

Follow AGENTS.md's source-first reading and shared-context maintenance contract.
For bounded work, start with the assigned issue, current delivery status,
`dev/source-contracts.md`, source Javadoc and relevant design/research sections.
Read the full planning entries for new scope, cross-cutting decisions or missing
design context. Update affected source contracts and planning evidence together.

- Read `versions.properties` and use the checked-in Gradle wrapper and `mcdev.cmd`.
- Select installed skills by task: `minecraft-plugin-development` for plugin work,
  `paper-runtime-validation` for server verification, and `paper-threading-review`
  for threading/lifecycle changes. Read only relevant skills.
- Use Context7 when available for unfamiliar/version-sensitive API documentation;
  verify that answers match the pinned API. Fall back to official docs/signatures.
- A successful build or MockBukkit test does not prove real Paper or player behavior.
  Follow the contract's proportionate checks and report what was actually verified.
